      "title": "To John Murray 16 [July 1845]",
      "header_text": [
        "To John Murray 16 [July 1845]Down Bromley Kent16 Wednesday | (after post-time)"
      ],
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "text": "I sent the M.S. to Mess. Clowes on the 7th & since then I have had only three sheets. I urged him to send me a sheet a day, stating the reason that my health is uncertain & that I would not on any account suffer, what I did last time, when, being unwell, I had to look over three or four sheets the last day.— Now I see Ms. Clowes is running the same course this time & I write to inform you, that if the number shd fail being ready it will be exclusively the fault of Mess. Clowes for I cannot & will not exert myself again, if I chance to be unwell",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 2,
          "text": "Will you be so kind as to take the affair in your own hands with Mess. Clowes.",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 2"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 3,
          "text": "My dear Sir | Yours very faithfully | C. Darwin",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 3"
        }
      ],
      "excluded_body_annotations_and_salutations": [
        {
          "class": "salute",
          "text": "My dear Sir"
        }
      ],
      "body_container_count": 1,
      "used_whole_body_fallback": false,
      "editorial_summary": "Summary Sent MS [of second part of Journal of researches] to William Clowes [printer] on the 7th and has had only three sheets for correction. Asks JM to see to it that Messrs Clowes send a sheet a day, as CD’s health is uncertain, and he cannot do more at last moment if sheets accumulate.",
      "editorial_footnotes": "",
      "letter_container_present": true
    },
