      "title": "To John Murray [23 August 1845]",
      "header_text": [
        "To John Murray [23 August 1845]Down Bromley KentSaturday"
      ],
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "text": "I am really mortified to find that I have transgressed my limits again— I had in truth thought this part with the index wd have been 168 pages; I now find without the index it has run to 174. I am astonished at this & much vexed. I have had to rewrite two Chapters, & these have, I presume, been lengthened, though I have struck out many whole pages & discussions. I now send this proof sheet to ask, whether you wd like to strike out, my rather dull little account p. 486 of the C. of Good Hope (as explained for the Printers in the enclosed bit of paper) & this, with the closing up, will save four pages; & I think if the index, is in very small type, it will go in the six last pages of this last sheet.",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 2,
          "text": "The contents must, of course be on a separate half sheet.—",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 2"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 3,
          "text": "Please decide freely as you like, & send the sheets early on Monday to the Printers, requesting them to send me a revise, if possible, by the general Post on Monday night.—",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 3"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 4,
          "text": "I know how late it is, but I have worked like a slave & have not lost one half hour: I sent the index on last Thursday to the Printers & hope to have a proof tomorrow morning—",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 4"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 5,
          "text": "I will communicate with you again in a few days.",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 5"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 6,
          "text": "Part I has 176 pages",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 6"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 7,
          "text": "—— II has 160",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 7"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 8,
          "text": "—— III has, if index will go in & you strike out the C. of Good Hope 176 so that I have exceeded by one whole sheet, what I promised you, & very sorry I am.",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 8"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 9,
          "text": "Yours very faithfully | C. Darwin",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 9"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 10,
          "text": "I was gratifyed by seeing two most favourable notice, & an extract in the Gardeners Chronicle, evidently by Lindley, with whom I am not acquainted, except by correspondence.—",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 10"
        }
      ],
      "excluded_body_annotations_and_salutations": [
        {
          "class": "salute",
          "text": "My dear Sir"
        }
      ],
      "body_container_count": 1,
      "used_whole_body_fallback": false,
      "editorial_summary": "Summary Has again overrun his limits [in MS of third part of Journal of researches]. Sends JM a proof sheet of his account of Cape of Good Hope for decision whether to strike it out and save four pages. Favourable notice of Journal has appeared in Gardeners’ Chronicle.",
      "editorial_footnotes": "Footnotes1The third and final number of Journal of researches 2d ed.2The chapters in question were those on the Galápagos and Keeling Islands. The first included new information on the flora from Joseph Dalton Hooker and on the insects from George Robert Waterhouse. The Keeling Islands chapter was expanded by a detailed summary of CD’s theory of coral reefs.3The passages were omitted, but this number nevertheless came to 182 pages (Freeman 1977, p. 39).4Gardeners’ Chronicle and Agricultural Gazette, no. 32, 9 August 1845, p. 546; no. 33, 16 August 1845, p. 563.",
      "letter_container_present": true
    },
